<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What a host is told about the certificates widget before it ever draws one.

  Everything here that is also in counts_widget_info.xml means the same thing and is the same
  value, with one deliberate exception: the box this widget is placed in. The reasoning for the
  shared parts is in that file and is not repeated here; what follows is only what differs.

  ### The declared size and the resize floor are not the same figure

  minWidth and minHeight are what a host without a cell grid places the widget at, and
  targetCellWidth and targetCellHeight are what a host with one uses from Android 12 onwards. Both
  say 300 x 250 dp, which is the box that lists four certificates — a list of two is a list that
  mostly says "and more".

  The resize floor stays at 300 x 170 dp, which is a promise this widget keeps: at that size it
  lists two, measured in a real host view at three font scales. So the widget can be made as small
  as the counts widget, it is simply not placed that way.

  The cell figures follow the same proportion the counts widget's do — three cells of its width,
  one cell more of its height.

  ### The layout a host inflates before the first update

  The list layout for the box above, whose default texts say that nothing has loaded rather than
  showing a specimen certificate. A specimen would be a fabricated figure about somebody's
  infrastructure sitting in a widget picker.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="io.github.jellyforgedev.widgora.widget.config.WidgetConfigActivity"
    android:description="@string/widget_description_certificates"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_list"
    android:maxResizeHeight="320dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="640dp"
    android:minHeight="250dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="170dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="300dp"
    android:minWidth="300dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_list"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable" />
